  "limitations": [
    "Only FIVE held-out adulterant systems exist: a macro mean over five folds says little about systems beyond them; the spread across folds matters more than the mean.",
    "Brand imbalance is a confounder (walnut = Luhua only; soybean/peanut = 2 brands; rapeseed/corn = 3). Every test brand also appears in training under other adulterants, so a model can partly exploit brand-specific fluorescence; the Luhua-only sensitivity run removes this confound at the price of fewer samples.",
    "All spectra come from one instrument and one lab protocol; no cross-device claim.",
    "Samples are laboratory binary mixtures, not marketplace products. Not a certified test.",
    "Inductive mode only: no information from the held-out batch is used. Transductive (OT) numbers belong to M4 and must never be mixed with these.",
    "Predictions are scored unclipped; clipped-to-[0,1] metrics are reported separately.",
    "The protocol was frozen (ADR-013) before the held-out adulterants were scored; the M2 grids were widened once before freezing, using inner CV only (ADR-012)."
  ],
